      "problem": "Solve the inequality $10x - 4 > 16.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $4$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10x-4 & >16 \\\\ 10x-4+4 & >16+4 \\\\ 10x+0 & >20 \\\\ 10x & >20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $10{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10x & >20 \\\\ \\frac{10x}{10} & >\\frac{20}{10} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{10}x}{\\cancel{10}} & >2 \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x> 2.$",
